# Normalise line endings in the repository.
#
# The repo previously held a mix of LF and CRLF files, so any tool that
# rewrote a file could silently flip all of its line endings and turn a
# one-line edit into a whole-file diff. Git now stores every text file
# with LF; `text=auto` lets git decide what is text, so binaries
# (documentation/reference/*.docx, images, fonts) are left untouched.
#
# Working-copy endings are not forced: a Windows checkout still gets CRLF
# if core.autocrlf says so. Only what is committed is normalised.
* text=auto

# Document fixtures whose bytes the tests read directly -- left exactly as
# they are rather than normalised.
backend/tests/fixtures/*.rtf -text
